WEBVTT

00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:19.733
<i>What's this feeling I have,</i>
<i>as if I'm looking forward to...</i>

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:25.939
<i>... somebody firing off his</i>
<i>missiles and ending everything?</i>

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:31.378
<i>Is it a bad thing, or is this normal?</i>

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:37.884
<i>I can't figure it out on my</i>
<i>own, so somebody tell me!</i>

00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:43.490
<i>And that person I love has once again...</i>

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:49.930
<i>... gone far away without anybody noticing.</i>

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:56.103
<i>Where have my dreams gone since then?</i>

00:00:56.103 --> 00:01:01.775
<i>I could swear that they</i>
<i>were right here long ago.</i>

00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:07.814
<i>We had a love that set our hearts on fire.</i>

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:20.784
<i>Let's take back that feeling we had back then!</i>

00:01:51.358 --> 00:01:55.192
Oh, no... I fell asleep.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.665
I'm not in right now.

00:01:58.665 --> 00:02:03.170
- Leave a message after the beep.
- Oh, right, I left the machine on...

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.372
Sakuya? It's me, Tenchi.

00:02:05.372 --> 00:02:08.909
I went to your place yesterday, but
you weren't there, so I was wondering...

00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:11.945
<i>...if</i> anything was wrong.
- Tenchi came to see me!

00:02:11.945 --> 00:02:15.482
Well, I'll call again later. Bye.

00:02:15.482 --> 00:02:16.616
Tenchi!

00:02:16.616 --> 00:02:18.218
Sakuya?

00:02:18.218 --> 00:02:22.088
I just got back! What did you want?

00:02:22.088 --> 00:02:23.919
Nothing major.

00:02:25.091 --> 00:02:27.093
Wanna go somewhere
tomorrow and have some fun?

00:02:27.093 --> 00:02:30.063
Some fun? Sure, I'll go!

00:02:30.063 --> 00:02:34.167
Great! I'll be waiting at the
usual park tomorrow at 10, then!

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:36.837
Ten o'clock at the park, huh? Got it.

00:02:36.837 --> 00:02:38.305
I'll be there!

00:02:38.305 --> 00:02:41.001
I'll see you at the park tomorrow, then.

00:03:11.705 --> 00:03:15.742
It's true. It's just as you said.

00:03:15.742 --> 00:03:17.869
Just as I thought.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.886
That clears up all our little mysteries.

00:03:25.886 --> 00:03:28.655
You're going, then? To Tokyo?

00:03:28.655 --> 00:03:32.859
Yeah. I have to tell Tenchi
about this as soon as possible.

00:03:32.859 --> 00:03:35.729
In that case, I'll come with you.

00:03:35.729 --> 00:03:41.902
I knew I would have to
tell this to Tenchi one day.

00:03:41.902 --> 00:03:47.641
Besides, it is my role and duty
as the head of the Masaki house.

00:03:47.641 --> 00:03:50.337
All right. Let's go.

00:04:08.061 --> 00:04:10.196
Tenchi...

00:04:10.196 --> 00:04:12.187
Sakuya!

00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:15.259
Tenchi!

00:04:18.305 --> 00:04:20.674
Sorry I'm late.

00:04:20.674 --> 00:04:25.579
That's okay. I just got here myself.

00:04:25.579 --> 00:04:29.149
Where should we go, Sakuya?

00:04:29.149 --> 00:04:34.354
Come to think of it,
I've never asked you out, have I?

00:04:34.354 --> 00:04:36.481
So, where should we go?

00:04:38.525 --> 00:04:41.194
Um... Tenchi?

00:04:41.194 --> 00:04:44.898
I'm not sure if I can...

00:04:44.898 --> 00:04:48.435
Let's go to the station first and
decide where to go from there.

00:04:48.435 --> 00:04:50.198
Tenchi?

00:04:53.006 --> 00:04:54.906
Tenchi...

00:04:57.377 --> 00:05:00.814
I... I...

00:05:00.814 --> 00:05:02.907
I'd like to see the ocean!

00:05:05.085 --> 00:05:07.287
Okay! Let's go!

00:05:07.287 --> 00:05:08.982
Yeah!

00:05:24.037 --> 00:05:26.039
Damn, you're one persistent bastard...

00:05:26.039 --> 00:05:28.803
Nobody likes persistent guys!

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.517
Sorry, Ryoko. I don't like to get violent,

00:05:37.517 --> 00:05:43.223
but I can't let you go back to Earth.
Back to Tenchi Masaki.

00:05:43.223 --> 00:05:46.215
Oh? And why's that?

00:05:47.127 --> 00:05:50.797
It doesn't sound like it's
just out of jealousy over Tenchi.

00:05:50.797 --> 00:05:55.325
Hotsuma! What the
hell is happening on Earth?

00:05:59.039 --> 00:06:00.674
What good will knowing that do you?

00:06:00.674 --> 00:06:03.443
You'll die here, so it's
got nothing to do with you.

00:06:03.443 --> 00:06:06.079
You'll kill me?

00:06:06.079 --> 00:06:08.548
I don't think you know what
you've gotten yourself into...

00:06:08.548 --> 00:06:12.040
All right. No more kid gloves.

00:06:19.526 --> 00:06:20.823
What?!

00:06:36.843 --> 00:06:40.301
You're a washout as a lady-killer, Hotsuma.

00:06:41.915 --> 00:06:44.645
- Now you've done it...
- What the...?

00:06:52.158 --> 00:06:55.889
You're dead, Ryoko!

00:07:01.768 --> 00:07:04.566
Matori. Are you there, Matori?

00:07:06.606 --> 00:07:08.408
You called?

00:07:08.408 --> 00:07:13.113
It looks like the time has finally
come to make this world my country.

00:07:13.113 --> 00:07:15.548
The time I make my dreams come true.

00:07:15.548 --> 00:07:17.117
Congratulations.

00:07:17.117 --> 00:07:19.085
But before then...

00:07:20.653 --> 00:07:24.758
I want you to bring Sasami here.

00:07:24.758 --> 00:07:29.095
Oh, dear. Are you sure
that's such a good idea?

00:07:29.095 --> 00:07:33.199
She's cute, but she's our enemy.

00:07:33.199 --> 00:07:38.899
She may be happier if you killed
her with the others, don't you think?

00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:41.541
Oo, scary!

00:07:41.541 --> 00:07:43.907
Very well, as you wish!

00:07:48.548 --> 00:07:50.482
Now, all that's left is to...

00:08:02.428 --> 00:08:03.963
This feels great!

00:08:03.963 --> 00:08:05.624
It sure does.

00:08:07.901 --> 00:08:10.737
Thanks, Tenchi.

00:08:10.737 --> 00:08:13.540
It's kinda nice, not being alone.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:16.409
I get really relaxed when it's like this.

00:08:16.409 --> 00:08:23.216
I don't really know why, but I get
the feeling that I've always been alone.

00:08:23.216 --> 00:08:25.418
Oh.

00:08:25.418 --> 00:08:27.784
Say, Tenchi?

00:08:39.065 --> 00:08:41.568
There's one summer memory!

00:08:41.568 --> 00:08:45.732
If I don't have any memories, I should
make a lot of 'em from now on, right?

00:08:47.073 --> 00:08:48.563
Sure!

00:08:49.375 --> 00:08:51.468
Let's go, Tenchi!

00:09:06.993 --> 00:09:08.895
Look what you did to our ship!

00:09:08.895 --> 00:09:11.164
Somebody could've been hurt!

00:09:11.164 --> 00:09:13.333
If you're going to surrender peacefully, fine!

00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:16.769
But if you're going to
resist, we won't hold back!

00:09:16.769 --> 00:09:20.206
Kiyone, should we really
just go and arrest him?

00:09:20.206 --> 00:09:23.009
I mean, we are on vacation and all...

00:09:23.009 --> 00:09:27.380
Now look here... Our shuttle was
shot down, so that doesn't matter, right?

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:30.316
Damn! This is the worst vacation in history!

00:09:30.316 --> 00:09:35.321
Oh, you were on vacation?
I didn't ruin it, did I?

00:09:35.321 --> 00:09:40.393
Who the hell are you?!
You saved us earlier, didn't you?

00:09:40.393 --> 00:09:43.663
Oh, I had my reasons.

00:09:43.663 --> 00:09:48.601
Today, I'm here on
Yugi's orders to take your lives.

00:09:48.601 --> 00:09:50.770
"Yugi"?

00:09:50.770 --> 00:09:54.941
Now I get it! You two are in cahoots!

00:09:54.941 --> 00:09:56.342
What are you after?

00:09:56.342 --> 00:10:00.813
Oh, this and that. If you manage
to beat me, maybe I'll tell you.

00:10:00.813 --> 00:10:04.010
I see. Well, don't cry
to me if you get hurt!

00:10:08.388 --> 00:10:10.219
You can't hit me!

00:10:13.059 --> 00:10:14.127
Huh?

00:10:14.127 --> 00:10:18.264
Hey, what are you waiting for?!
Start shooting, Mihoshi!

00:10:18.264 --> 00:10:19.822
Okay.

00:10:29.042 --> 00:10:31.244
Got him!

00:10:31.244 --> 00:10:32.802
No way...

00:10:39.686 --> 00:10:43.790
I was worried that something might happen,

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:47.694
but nothing did.

00:10:47.694 --> 00:10:49.457
Welcome back!

00:11:13.553 --> 00:11:17.455
You have something to tell me, Grandpa?

00:11:18.725 --> 00:11:20.026
So, you know.

00:11:20.026 --> 00:11:22.290
Well, sort of.

00:11:23.663 --> 00:11:26.063
Well, I guess I'll start.

00:11:26.766 --> 00:11:29.836
First, I told you earlier that the
Masaki Shrine had been attacked

00:11:29.836 --> 00:11:33.706
and that everyone had split up, right?

00:11:33.706 --> 00:11:34.841
Right.

00:11:34.841 --> 00:11:38.544
As I thought, it looks like
it was due to enemy action.

00:11:38.544 --> 00:11:40.179
What do you mean?

00:11:40.179 --> 00:11:43.148
Tenchi, do you remember this place?

00:11:43.983 --> 00:11:48.221
Aren't those the ruins we found in
North Okutama when my class went there?

00:11:48.221 --> 00:11:50.223
I did some checking and got a big surprise!

00:11:50.223 --> 00:11:52.592
It turns out that they're from Jurai!

00:11:52.592 --> 00:11:56.029
Jurai? As in, where
Ayeka and Sasami are from?!

00:11:56.029 --> 00:11:58.831
Yeah. But they're pretty old.

00:11:58.831 --> 00:12:01.467
What are Juraian ruins doing on Earth?

00:12:01.467 --> 00:12:03.603
It's not a ruin.

00:12:03.603 --> 00:12:06.572
It's shaped like a coffin,
but in terms of function...

00:12:06.572 --> 00:12:08.441
...it's really a cold-sleep capsule.

00:12:08.441 --> 00:12:10.743
But it's empty...

00:12:10.743 --> 00:12:14.480
That's right. The person
who was in there has woken up

00:12:14.480 --> 00:12:16.549
and has been up to no good, that's why.

00:12:16.549 --> 00:12:19.419
Don't tell me that the person
who attacked our shrine was...

00:12:19.419 --> 00:12:24.123
Yep. When I traced the
bio-signature back on the time axis,

00:12:24.123 --> 00:12:25.925
it led right back to this coffin.

00:12:25.925 --> 00:12:28.361
The mastermind of all
those Guardian Spirit incidents

00:12:28.361 --> 00:12:29.829
was probably the
person who was in there, too.

00:12:29.829 --> 00:12:31.397
But who the heck is it?

00:12:31.397 --> 00:12:34.889
I bet you've met her
before somewhere, Tenchi.

00:12:36.803 --> 00:12:38.504
Her name's Yugi.

00:12:38.504 --> 00:12:40.563
"Yugi"?

00:12:45.445 --> 00:12:49.749
Yugi? Sasami's friend, Yugi?!

00:12:49.749 --> 00:12:53.319
That's impossible! It's got to
be some kind of mistake, Washu!

00:12:53.319 --> 00:12:57.223
I dug around in the databank reserved
for use by the Juraian royal family

00:12:57.223 --> 00:12:59.492
and came across this.

00:12:59.492 --> 00:13:05.031
She... Yugi is a mutant
created 3,600 years ago on Jurai.

00:13:05.031 --> 00:13:07.033
"Mutant"?

00:13:07.033 --> 00:13:09.569
It looks like she's a
mutant that was created

00:13:09.569 --> 00:13:12.772
through research into a
super-energy called the Power of Jurai.

00:13:12.772 --> 00:13:15.241
She tried to use her
powerful spiritual powers

00:13:15.241 --> 00:13:18.845
to create her own kingdom on Jurai.

00:13:18.845 --> 00:13:23.116
But her plans were foiled by
the powers of the royal house,

00:13:23.116 --> 00:13:26.319
and she was sealed into that
coffin-shaped cold-sleep capsule

00:13:26.319 --> 00:13:29.914
and banished forever into deep space.

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:33.826
So, the coffin that was
drifting in space came down

00:13:33.826 --> 00:13:35.795
here on Earth by some fluke?

00:13:35.795 --> 00:13:39.365
Yugi probably hopes to fulfill the
dream she couldn't fulfil on Jurai,

00:13:39.365 --> 00:13:43.302
to found a country of
her own, here on Earth.

00:13:43.302 --> 00:13:45.371
But why?

00:13:45.371 --> 00:13:49.075
Why did she try to split us up?

00:13:49.075 --> 00:13:51.373
This is why.

00:13:52.111 --> 00:13:54.978
One of Mom's gems!

00:13:56.749 --> 00:14:00.150
I'll tell you about that.

00:14:08.694 --> 00:14:13.799
I wonder if Tenchi's home yet?

00:14:13.799 --> 00:14:15.201
Planetary Defenders?

00:14:15.201 --> 00:14:19.438
Yes. It is we of the Masaki family
who protect the world from evil ones

00:14:19.438 --> 00:14:24.277
and the will of the gods
that we be the Defenders.

00:14:24.277 --> 00:14:28.014
Generation after generation, we have
obeyed that mandate and served the gods,

00:14:28.014 --> 00:14:33.686
fighting evil behind the scenes
of history and protecting this world.

00:14:33.686 --> 00:14:35.421
Those gems are the symbol
of the Planetary Defenders,

00:14:35.421 --> 00:14:38.524
which has been passed
down in the Masaki family.

00:14:38.524 --> 00:14:41.460
Mom's gems had that
kind of secret behind them?

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:45.631
These gems are probably a
solid form of Earth's bio-energy.

00:14:45.631 --> 00:14:48.935
When we hold them,
there's not much of an effect,

00:14:48.935 --> 00:14:52.138
but if someone in resonance with
Earth's specific vibration uses them,

00:14:52.138 --> 00:14:54.307
it'll manifest an incredible power.

00:14:54.307 --> 00:14:56.375
And that's the Masaki clan?

00:14:56.375 --> 00:14:58.678
Yes. Exactly.

00:14:58.678 --> 00:15:00.213
Then what's with this light?

00:15:00.213 --> 00:15:02.081
A warning.

00:15:02.081 --> 00:15:06.052
When all the gems are assembled,
they'll manifest a special power

00:15:06.052 --> 00:15:08.120
that can defeat an evil one.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.958
But because those of us who
have the gems have been scattered,

00:15:11.958 --> 00:15:14.760
that power's been weakened.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:18.297
So that's why she's
been trying to break us up!

00:15:18.297 --> 00:15:20.666
You've been watching the news, right?

00:15:20.666 --> 00:15:22.668
Washu, don't tell me that...

00:15:22.668 --> 00:15:25.605
Right. Yugi's country.

00:15:25.605 --> 00:15:29.275
It's in another dimension right now,
but it's only a matter of time

00:15:29.275 --> 00:15:32.778
before she breaks the dimension
barrier and brings it into this world.

00:15:32.778 --> 00:15:36.515
What should we do, Washu? Grandpa?

00:15:36.515 --> 00:15:39.885
It's unfortunate, but
there's nothing we can do.

00:15:39.885 --> 00:15:43.556
We could do something if
we had all the gems together,

00:15:43.556 --> 00:15:50.029
but since three of them aren't
on Earth, it's a bit of a problem!

00:15:50.029 --> 00:15:55.763
It's my fault. All this happened
because I went to Tokyo!

00:15:56.702 --> 00:15:58.271
Tenchi...

00:15:58.271 --> 00:16:01.968
Actually, there's one other
thing that I have to tell you.

00:16:08.581 --> 00:16:11.641
So, you've finally come, Yugi!

00:16:13.219 --> 00:16:16.389
Be careful, Princess!

00:16:16.389 --> 00:16:18.186
I know!

00:16:20.826 --> 00:16:22.760
What?!

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:26.432
Wh-What in the world...?

00:16:26.432 --> 00:16:27.967
Where will she attack from?

00:16:27.967 --> 00:16:30.026
Sister!

00:16:30.736 --> 00:16:33.105
Sasami, stay inside!

00:16:33.105 --> 00:16:35.174
Sister...

00:16:35.174 --> 00:16:36.869
Princess!

00:16:42.748 --> 00:16:45.911
So, you've finally shown yourself!

00:16:48.054 --> 00:16:49.722
You're not Yugi!

00:16:49.722 --> 00:16:52.124
I'm Matori.

00:16:52.124 --> 00:16:53.859
Yugi's servant.

00:16:53.859 --> 00:16:56.095
Yugi's servant?

00:16:56.095 --> 00:17:00.166
Come with me, Miss.
Yugi's waiting for you.

00:17:00.166 --> 00:17:01.967
Yugi's waiting for me?

00:17:01.967 --> 00:17:07.273
You want to see her, too, right?
I'll take you there. To Yugi.

00:17:07.273 --> 00:17:11.403
What are you saying?! I won't permit it!

00:17:13.479 --> 00:17:18.617
If you don't want to be hurt,
you shouldn't interfere, Princess.

00:17:18.617 --> 00:17:21.787
That's exactly what
I was about to say to you!

00:17:21.787 --> 00:17:23.756
Azaka! Kamidake!

00:17:23.756 --> 00:17:26.025
Activate ultimate defense system!

00:17:26.025 --> 00:17:27.617
- Yes, Ma'am!
- Yes, Ma'am!

00:17:32.331 --> 00:17:36.700
Well, what will you do?
If you're going to run, now's the time.

00:17:39.638 --> 00:17:42.869
That's exactly what I was about to say to you.

00:17:43.509 --> 00:17:46.307
Arise, Guardian Spirits!

00:17:51.384 --> 00:17:52.976
What did she say?

00:17:55.454 --> 00:18:00.221
If you value your life, be a
good girl and hand over Sasami.

00:18:09.835 --> 00:18:12.905
Maybe we shouldn't have told him.

00:18:12.905 --> 00:18:14.805
Tenchi...

00:18:26.886 --> 00:18:30.189
It can't! It can't be!

00:18:30.189 --> 00:18:32.324
You know this girl, I assume?

00:18:32.324 --> 00:18:33.325
Sure.

00:18:33.325 --> 00:18:35.828
She isn't human.

00:18:35.828 --> 00:18:38.864
You're kidding, right, Washu?

00:18:38.864 --> 00:18:43.502
We're friends, Washu, but there are
some things you shouldn't joke about!

00:18:43.502 --> 00:18:47.973
I'll apply a filter and
display only the bio-energy.

00:18:47.973 --> 00:18:51.670
See for yourself. This is what she really is.

00:19:02.121 --> 00:19:04.146
Tenchi...

00:19:10.029 --> 00:19:13.699
Thank you for all your hard work, Sakuya.

00:19:13.699 --> 00:19:16.101
I've come for you, Sakuya.

00:19:16.101 --> 00:19:19.901
The time for my dreams to
come true has finally come.

00:19:23.209 --> 00:19:26.612
Wh-What? What're you talking about?

00:19:26.612 --> 00:19:30.716
Come, Sakuya. Come back to me.

00:19:30.716 --> 00:19:32.384
Who are you?

00:19:32.384 --> 00:19:37.223
Sakuya, you're part
of me. You're my reflection.

00:19:37.223 --> 00:19:40.659
No! Tenchi!

00:19:41.894 --> 00:19:43.896
Help me!

00:19:43.896 --> 00:19:46.364
No!

00:19:51.971 --> 00:19:55.168
Sakuya! Sakuya, open up!

00:20:00.846 --> 00:20:06.807
You're a little late, Tenchi Masaki.
I've taken back my reflection.

00:20:10.256 --> 00:20:13.092
The preparations are now all complete.

00:20:13.092 --> 00:20:17.586
It's only a matter of time before
this world becomes my country.

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:39.218
Tenchi? Thanks for today. I had a great time.

00:20:39.218 --> 00:20:41.587
I've made up my mind.

00:20:41.587 --> 00:20:46.258
I'm gonna stop moping around just
because I don't have any memories.

00:20:46.258 --> 00:20:53.299
I mean, I'm here to love you.
That's the feeling I get, somehow.

00:20:53.299 --> 00:21:00.573
Tenchi, I fell in love with you more and more.

00:21:00.573 --> 00:21:02.768
Sakuya...

00:21:22.027 --> 00:21:34.963
<i>You always talk to me so openly,</i>

00:21:37.109 --> 00:21:51.479
<i>but my heart feels</i>
<i>happier than anyone else's.</i>

00:21:54.326 --> 00:22:07.364
<i>Please don't smile at me with</i>
<i>that kind look, it's just too painful.</i>

00:22:10.476 --> 00:22:26.154
<i>I hope I can be more forward</i>
<i>and let you know how I feel...</i>

00:22:42.474 --> 00:22:47.813
The city... Everyone's being
swallowed up into a grey world!

00:22:47.813 --> 00:22:50.516
It really is you who's behind all this, Yugi!

00:22:50.516 --> 00:22:52.718
I can't believe it!

00:22:52.718 --> 00:22:56.622
You seemed to be having so
much fun when you were with me!

00:22:56.622 --> 00:22:59.058
Why are you doing
all these horrible things?!

00:22:59.058 --> 00:23:04.163
Let's all be friends! Please, Yugi!

00:23:04.163 --> 00:23:10.932
Next time on <i>Tenchi in Tokyo:</i>
"The End of Time."
